docs/guide/export.md:307:- **Remove Background.** A clip with Remove Background is drawn as the person alone in every frame of the file. Its person masks are made on this Mac as soon as the cutout is set, and an export waits, showing "Preparing…", until every mask it draws is made — GIF and APNG too. If they cannot be made, the export fails with "Clip *n*'s person masks could not be made: …" and writes no file.
docs/guide/export.md:308:- **The gate, the leveller and the de-esser.** Their thresholds follow each clip's measured loudness, and the leveller works from the clip's speech too, so an export waits, showing "Preparing…", until every gated, levelled or de-essed clip in it has been measured. If a measurement has not landed after five minutes, the export fails with "Clip *n*'s loudness or speech has not been measured yet, so its gate, leveller and de-esser cannot be set. Wait for their Status rows to show the clip's loudness, then export again." (see [Audio](audio.md#gate)).
